From 9b1ae9c8b2798839c71d0bf0016f87368e9fedcf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jakub Jelen <jjelen@redhat.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 09:06:52 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Update the upstream signing key

Refresh Public-Key from keyservers/WKD: same certificate(s), with
self-signatures our copy was missing.
The commands are in the comment above its Source line.
Public-Key was in the lookaside cache, which a pull request cannot
update, so it moves into git (dropped from sources).

The current key is needed to verify the release signature with
openpgpverify (sqv), which checks that the key was valid when the
release was signed.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
---
 .gitignore      |   1 -
 Public-Key      | Bin 0 -> 24270 bytes
 mingw-pcre.spec |   4 ++++
 sources         |   1 -
 4 files changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 Public-Key

diff --git a/.gitignore b/.gitignore
index 1288990..33862c4 100644
--- a/.gitignore
+++ b/.gitignore
@@ -9,4 +9,3 @@
 /pcre-8.43.tar.bz2
 /pcre-8.45.tar.bz2
 /pcre-8.45.tar.bz2.sig
-/Public-Key
diff --git a/Public-Key b/Public-Key
new file mode 100644
